# ==============================================================
# StrictDocStarter .gitignore
# ==============================================================

# --- Claude / AI assistant (never commit) ---
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude.json
prompt.md

# --- Private / internal working docs (kept local, not published) ---
in-private-work/

# --- StrictDoc generated HTML / cache (strictdoc server / export) ---
#
# Only output/strictdoc/ is excluded, never output/ itself: that folder may well
# hold something its author put there on purpose, and a rule that swallows it
# deletes their work from Git's view without saying so. The launcher writes to
# <project>/output/strictdoc/ (FR-1160) and the advice it prints names the same
# path (FR-1161), so everything this repository generates is covered.
#
# ** rather than a leading slash because this file sits above the projects
# rather than inside one: the samples are six project folders under samples/.
#
# Output that lands anywhere else is left visible on purpose. `strictdoc export`
# without --output-dir scatters _cache/ and html/ directly into output/, and
# `strictdoc server` writes output/server/. Seeing those in `git status` is the
# signal that a command was run the wrong way; hiding them would only make the
# mistake quieter.
**/output/strictdoc/

# --- JSON exported by try-json-query-{en,ja}.bat (regenerated on every run) ---
exported-json/

# --- Scratch export folder used by the walkthroughs in docs/ ---
# docs/03-sdoc-json-queries.md and docs/queries/ tell the reader to export a
# sample here before running a query. It is regenerated on demand and is no more
# source than exported-json/ above.
out/

# --- GitHub Pages build (.github/workflows/publish-samples.yml, CI-only) ---
site/

# --- Python bytecode / cache / temp execution files ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# --- Python build / packaging / virtualenv (local tooling) ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- User-generated config (templates are committed instead) ---
setup.config.json
server.config.json
uninstall.config.json
env-report.json

# --- Runtime logs (setup.log, launch.log, and any transient *.log) ---
*.log

# --- Px local proxy config ---
px.ini

# --- Temp / build artifacts ---
/temp/
*.zip

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
*.tmp
